1
00:00:00,248 --> 00:00:02,178
(Prof Sharpe:)He was convinced that calorie
restriction was the key

2
00:00:02,183 --> 00:00:03,753
(Prof Sharpe:)to living forever.

3
00:00:03,752 --> 00:00:05,322
(Raj:)Does it work?

4
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:06,950
(Howard:)Seriously?

5
00:00:06,955 --> 00:00:09,655
(Raj:)Well, he could have been hit
by a bus. You don't know.

6
00:00:11,159 --> 00:00:13,089
(Prof Sharpe:)Sorry it's not more interesting.

7
00:00:13,094 --> 00:00:15,194
(Prof Sharpe:)On the bright side,
you didn't have to listen

8
00:00:15,196 --> 00:00:17,926
(Prof Sharpe:)to his stomach growl
for 35 years.

9
00:00:17,932 --> 00:00:20,032
(Leonard:)So, was there anything
that Professor Abbott worked on

10
00:00:20,035 --> 00:00:23,205
(Leonard:)during his life that came close
to an accomplishment?

11
00:00:23,204 --> 00:00:26,644
(Prof Sharpe:)To be honest, his research
never amounted to anything.

12
00:00:26,641 --> 00:00:28,611
(Howard:)Oh.
You were his
colleague.

13
00:00:28,610 --> 00:00:29,640
(Raj:)How did your research turn out?

14
00:00:29,644 --> 00:00:31,644
(Raj:)Great. Hey, this is
the apartment you get

15
00:00:31,646 --> 00:00:33,746
(Raj:)when you win a Nobel.

16
00:00:34,949 --> 00:00:37,049
(Raj:)Well, you could be very frugal.

17
00:00:37,052 --> 00:00:39,352
(Raj:)I'm getting a little tired
of everybody's sarcasm.

18
00:00:42,691 --> 00:00:44,891
(Bernadette:)I'm not a bully.

19
00:00:44,893 --> 00:00:47,123
(Bernadette:)I mean, maybe I come
off a little strong,

20
00:00:47,128 --> 00:00:49,128
(Bernadette:)but that's only because my
dad raised me to be tough

21
00:00:49,130 --> 00:00:50,500
(Bernadette:)and not to take
crap from anybody.

22
00:00:50,498 --> 00:00:53,868
(Penny:)No. That's fine, but there's
a difference between being tough

23
00:00:53,868 --> 00:00:57,138
(Penny:)and telling your friend her new
pants look like a saggy diaper.

24
00:00:59,140 --> 00:01:01,240
(Bernadette:)I did say that, didn't I?

